                    {
                        "sense_id": "30ead075-698a-38ed-9edd-5c065c5528ba",
                        "entry_id": "ac55a901-707c-3f23-a6cc-1d432534bbbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make tender."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e7e6e9c-4c9f-48c4-86d9-0e4695b6560e",
                                "sense_id": "30ead075-698a-38ed-9edd-5c065c5528ba",
                                "text": "Entendered by distress, she easily yielded to the pensive manners of her companions and to the serene uniformity of a monastic life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93f24011-95b9-401e-b792-6fc4f4f713ec",
                                "sense_id": "30ead075-698a-38ed-9edd-5c065c5528ba",
                                "text": "And fearing lest the torments he felt, might in some sort entender his wifes heart[…], he besought her to be pleased she might be caried into the next chamber, which was accordingly performed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0b61e99-3c97-42fa-83ea-540ce8aecc55",
                                "sense_id": "30ead075-698a-38ed-9edd-5c065c5528ba",
                                "text": "For whatsoever creates fear , or makes the spirit to dwell in a religious sadness , is apt to entender the spirit , and make it devout and pliant to any part of dut"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "09769940-4336-30f4-b585-8aeb19f45ad7",
                        "entry_id": "ac55a901-707c-3f23-a6cc-1d432534bbbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To treat with tenderness."
